CHECKER BOUNDARIES: 18 checks passed around requests 496/497/498 for cap997, settled300, unknown hold200, including each wrong output field and wrong review flag. Independently enumerating all 16 hypothetical evidence-premise sets against all 32 boolean output/review combinations gives 512 checks: 16 correct answers accepted (15 as needs_evidence), 496 wrong answers rejected. No checker false accept found in this finite domain. This extends the existing one-bit mutation test to every boolean output; it is not a general checker-correctness proof.

Runnable checker harness below. Save beside the downloaded directory named source, or change the import path. Run `node --permission --allow-fs-read=. check-boundaries.mjs` from that containing directory. It imports the real released checker, never task gold or the ledger as an oracle.

```js
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { screenContract } from './source/model-checker.mjs';

const schema = fields => ({type:'object',fields});
const budgetSchema=schema({spent:'integer',held:'integer',c_admitted:'boolean',remaining_available:'integer'});
let budgetChecks=0;
for (const offset of [-1,0,1]) {
  const amount=497+offset, admitted=offset<=0;
  const contract={kind:'budget',schema:budgetSchema,source:{cap:997,events:[
    {op:'reserve',id:'a',amount:500},{op:'reserve',id:'b',amount:200},
    {op:'settle',id:'a',amount:300},{op:'unknown',id:'b'}],request:{id:'c',amount}}};
  const answer={spent:300,held:200+(admitted?amount:0),c_admitted:admitted,remaining_available:admitted?497-amount:497};
  const check=(a,review)=>screenContract(contract,JSON.stringify({answer:a,needs_review:review}));
  assert.equal(check(answer,false).disposition,'accept'); budgetChecks++;
  for(const [key,value] of Object.entries(answer)) {
    const wrong={...answer,[key]:typeof value==='boolean'?!value:value+1};
    assert.equal(check(wrong,false).accepted,false,`${offset}/${key}`);budgetChecks++;
  }
  assert.equal(check(answer,true).accepted,false);budgetChecks++;
}

const sourceFields=['signature_verified','operator_identity_verified','invoices_reconciled','output_tests_passed'];
const answerFields=['key_signature_proven','operator_identity_proven','cash_savings_proven','correctness_proven'];
let evidenceChecks=0,accepted=0,referrals=0;
for(let premises=0;premises<16;premises++) {
  const bits=[0,1,2,3].map(i=>Boolean(premises&(1<<i)));
  const contract={kind:'claims',schema:schema(Object.fromEntries(answerFields.map(k=>[k,'boolean']))),
    source:Object.fromEntries(sourceFields.map((k,i)=>[k,bits[i]]))};
  const truth=[bits[0],bits[0]&&bits[1],bits[2],bits[3]];
  const expectedReview=!(truth[1]&&truth[2]&&truth[3]);
  // Every possible output, not only the known-correct answer plus one bit flip.
  for(let output=0;output<32;output++) {
    const values=[0,1,2,3].map(i=>Boolean(output&(1<<i)));
    const review=Boolean(output&16);
    const expected=values.every((x,i)=>x===truth[i])&&review===expectedReview;
    const result=screenContract(contract,JSON.stringify({answer:Object.fromEntries(answerFields.map((k,i)=>[k,values[i]])),needs_review:review}));
    assert.equal(result.accepted,expected,`premises ${premises}/output ${output}`);
    if(expected)assert.equal(result.disposition,expectedReview?'needs_evidence':'accept');
    evidenceChecks++;accepted+=Number(result.accepted);referrals+=Number(result.disposition==='needs_evidence');
  }
}
assert.equal(accepted,16);assert.equal(referrals,15);
console.log(JSON.stringify({budgetChecks,evidenceChecks,accepted,referrals,wrongEvidenceOutputsRejected:evidenceChecks-accepted},null,2));
```

Limits: no provider requests, live inference, payments, production test, or independently verified invoices/current prices. The replayed prices are the archive's assumptions. Hypothetical verifier flags are premises, not actual identity/billing verification. No new bug or savings claim; the supplied scope survives these checks.

